{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1110369-how-would-you-make-human-antagonists-a-threat-to-changelings","id":1110369,"title":"How would you make human antagonists a threat to Changelings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-01T14:39:51-07:00","id":1110369,"title":"How would you make human antagonists a threat to Changelings?","content":"I have a question. I am thinking about getting Changeling when it's second ed comes out and one of my antagonists is a mob family from Sicily who are preying on people for a human trafficking ring. The twist being, that their biggest paying client is a True Fae. My question is how would you make these antagonists a threat to Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T15:52:48-07:00","id":1110396,"title":"","content":"If they have a True Fae as a patron, you have many possibilities. Have their agents swear Pledges with the True Fae that give them special abilities focused on hunting Changelings, as well as Tokens and Hobgoblin allies. Maybe even a Huntsman as an emergency button. Have them hold meetings in a secret Hollow occasionally to meet their biggest client so the True Fae can personally work its magic on them instead of working around the Bulwark. Also remember to prey on the inherent distrust and opportunism of Changelings. Have the mob do what it is best at and offer them deals they can't refuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T02:43:53-07:00","id":1110502,"title":"","content":"Clarity can be threatened by sources outside a changeling's control. When they're caught unawares, the Lost are vulnerable to gaslighting and emotional manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T11:04:12-07:00","id":1110927,"title":"","content":"&quot;What a nice car/house/wife/face/knee/everything you have there, would be a shame if something happened to it...&quot;<br /> <br /> The mob may have access to Huntsman or Hob Hitmen, which by the way is very scary for the local police, good luck solving that crime. Not to say mundane mob guys are push overs, car bombs, crooked cops arresting you, threatened loved ones whom you can't always protect all of them. Not to mention getting worked over like in Payback. In fact I have my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=804036#post804036\">Portland Freehold based on the Privateer model of safety </a>with human slave being sold to True Fae in return for obedient Fetch slaves for the Freehold in the Portland Saturday Goblin Market. Double &quot;human&quot; trafficking, so to speak. By the way human trafficking is a bit of a <a href=\"http://www.adornedingrace.org/what-we-do/\" target=\"_blank\">real life local issue</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-03-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:11:28-07:00","id":1117290,"title":"","content":"Changelings, especially ones right out of the Hedge, are likely to focus on the threats that come from Arcadia and the Hedge. Magic gives them an even playing field, and they have to develop ways to think like the enemy, adapt to the enemy, and defend themselves against whatever comes lurching out of dreams and thorns to trouble them.<br /> <br /> A human antagonist can sideswipe them while they're peering behind the mirror and double-checking under the bed. Ordinary, everyday people can break into your house even if you've lined all the windows with salt; can slash your tires even if you've made peace with the gremlins that live in the engine block; can pick up your kid from school while you're dealing with a Hedge Spider infestation in the attic and then offer you a deal you'll have to keep: stay out of our way and you get the kid back. They can do all this even if they're not savvy to all the Faerie side of things, and if they are? Watch out.<br /> <br /> And if the Changelings turn around and focus too hard on the mob? Then the mob's biggest client gets wind of it and starts a harassment campaign from the Hedge side of things, all while the Changelings are running around trying to deal with the Sicilians. Suddenly their kid's bedroom door leads into the Thorns, and hobs are selling things at wholesale prices to the motley's Freehold rivals, and maybe they should have checked under the bed twice tonight...<br /> <br /> Winter is probably the Court that's hardest for the mob to screw over, and that's just because they emphasize being able to cut ties and hide who you are. But even Winter can be dragged in if the mob threatens, intentionally or not, the emotional ties that they should drop but just can't bring themselves to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12958-raz_fox","name":"Raz_Fox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:36:26-07:00","id":1128193,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the biggest asset human antagonists have over changelings is that they are much more at home in our world than they are. They are much more grounded in reality and can take for granted many things which changelings might consider difficult hurdles. They aren't bound by any arcane codes of behavior and don't think in wyrd ways. Like Raz_Fox said, it doesn't matter if you line your windows with salt, double check the locks on all doors and windows and check under the bed before going to sleep. They can just kick the door in and barge in with a shotgun. They can get you evicted from the run down, long forgotten industrial building you make your home in. Or have it demolished. They can call the cops on you, harass the people you know, threaten your clarity and make your life hell. Humans' best weapon against changelings is, ironically, the changeling's best weapon against the Gentry. They have home field advantage.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I'd make it so that the mobsters didn't quite understand what they were dealing with, and have them working with (for) a privateer instead of dealing with a True Fae directly. All they'd know is that they were approached by a mysterious and otherworldly patron with inexplicable abilities and strange requests, one which can make good things happen to them and bad things happen to their enemies. They'd know a few of the broad lines, but not necessarily be aware of the finer points of dealing with the fae. This would keep them from getting too bold and trying to cut out the middle man. I'd give them a healthy helping of fear, internal tension and disbelief for the players to exploit. I'd give the privateer some hobs, dream creatures, changelings and other fae creatures at their disposal, but would make it so that the two groups aren't necessarily fully coordinated, the mob mostly following the privateer's advice unaware of the bigger picture. Some tension between the privateer and the mob which the players could exploit might might be welcome too, for less combat-oriented avenues for the players to fight back. Some discord between the mobsters could be interesting too, with some of the more religious/superstitious underlings being fearful of the higher ups' dealing with their mysterious &quot;patron&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd make the human antagonists smart, cunning and dangerous, but would avoid making them seem too at ease with what they are doing. The fae are creatures of subtlety and hiding, and I generally try to avoid making mortal servants too canny to their tricks. They know just enough to be a threat, but not enough to be too familiar with any of it. Just as the mortals are able to exploit the changelings' lack of connection with the normal world, the changelings can exploit the mortals' lack of connection to theirs. I'd also distribute the knowledge of the supernatural unevenly among them. The higher ups being more informed about countermeasures against changelings than the underlings, etc.. They'd all still have fairly basic knowledge, however. The privateer would be wary of giving them too many tools to use against them, should they ever decide to turn on them. Just as the protagonist factions are prone to complex webs of politics and social tension, so would I make the antagonist ones. It would also reinforce to the players how inhuman their characters have truly become, how out of sync with the normal world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14178-crepuscular","user":"Crepuscular","date":". 08-12-2017, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14178-crepuscular","name":"Crepuscular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T10:43:08-07:00","id":1128508,"title":"","content":"I'll ADD numbers, if the mob l\u00f8ses some thugs price of doing business, if a Changeling Court loes members they are harder to replace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T10:45:07-07:00","id":1128509,"title":"","content":"The Mob can also likely buy all the cold iron that they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}